From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:18:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Play the AdLib on the DS sound hardware

opl.c replaces the MAME OPL2 emulator, which took most of the ARM9: every
OPL channel is a hardware channel looping one period of the waveform its
two FM operators make, at its pitch, with the envelopes, key scaling and
levels of the MAME emulator done in software at about 780 Hz.
